                <pb facs="0817" n="691" sameAs="frus:frus1925v01/pg691"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">893.5045/156: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to
                        the Ambassador in Great Britain</hi> (<hi
                            rendition="#italic">Houghton</hi>)</head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1925-08-05T13:00:00-04:00"><hi rendition="#italic">August 5,
                                1925—1 p.m.</hi></date></dateline></opener>
                <p>248. Your 245, August 4, 4 p.m. Instructions are being sent to American
                    Diplomatic representatives at Brussels, Copenhagen, The Hague, Lisbon, Madrid,
                    Stockholm and Oslo to consult with their British colleagues and if necessary to
                    support them as requested by informing the Foreign Offices of those countries
                    that this country has consented to the British proposal for the judicial
                    inquiry, it being understood that the judicial commission will include a Chinese
                    jurist.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Kellogg</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
